From ec3bcdc9f3cff5ade17cc42010b83d5aaa1e87c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:17:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Guest Portal: exempt from Gatekeeper, passcode at creation,
 safer answers; Wireless Log

- Gatekeeper leaves a Guest Portal network alone: its sign-in is the gate, and its devices are not
  held or listed (rc/gatekeeper.c, gkd). Isolation from the LAN stays the network's own setting.
- The Guest Portal wizard takes the passcode when the portal is created.
- lighttpd: the portal's answer to a sign-in request is sent as plain text, nosniff, with a closed
  CSP (it echoed the query as a page). The portal secret is read the same way by both halves of
  the sign-in; rc gives each router its own (the rc commit).
- Wireless Log: the main network is the main Guest Network Pro profile, not the first slot of a
  radio - a portal on a radio the main network does not use read "Main network". Chips: main
  green, Guest Network and Guest Portal blue, Customized amber; a profile type the stock page does
  not know reads Customized.
- Network page: the setup panel of every network type was cut off at the bottom; the frame follows
  the panel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
